                %li
                  %a{:href => "#for_coincident_nonabelian_dbranes"} For coincident (non-abelian) D-branes
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#on_flavor_branes_for_holographic_qcd"} On flavor branes for holographic QCD
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#HolographicSchwingerEffectReferences"} Holographic Schwinger effect
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#ReferencesDBIHigherCurvatureCorrections"} Higher curvature corrections to the DBI-action for D-branes
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#single_trace_observables_as_weight_systems_on_chord_diagrams"} Single trace observables as weight systems on chord diagrams
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#brane_intersections_as_dbispikesbions"} Brane intersections as DBI-spikes/BIons
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            What is known as
            %em Born-Infeld theory
            (
            %a{:href => "#BornInfeld34"}> Born &amp;Infeld 1934
            , often also attributed to
            %a{:href => "#Dirac62"} Dirac 1962
            and abbreviated “DBI theory”) is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation"} deformation
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theory+%28physics%29"} theory
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            which coincides with ordinary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetism"} electromagnetism
            for small excitations of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            but is such that there is a maximal value for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            which can never be reached in a physical process.
          %p
            Just this theory happens to describe the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            on single
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            at low
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/energy"} energy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+string"} open
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitudes"} string scattering amplitudes
            (
            %a{:href => "#FradkinTseytlin85"}> Fradkin-Tseytlin 85
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#AbouelsaoodCallanNappiYost87"} Abouelsaood-Callan-Nappi-Yost 87
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Leigh89"} Leigh 89
          %p
            In this context the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            corresponding to Born-Infeld theory arises as the low-energy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/effective+action"} effective action
            on the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            = succeed "." do
              %em DBI-action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Green-Schwarz+action+functional"} Green-Schwarz action functional
            for super
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            = succeed "-summand" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nambu-Goto+action"} Nambu-Goto action
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+strength"} field strength
            of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+fields"} Chan-Paton gauge fields
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+brane"} coincident
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+enhancement"} gauge enhancement
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chan-Paton+gauge+field"} Chan-Paton gauge field
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-abelian+group"} non-abelian
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+group"} gauge group
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+fields"} gauge fields
            is expected to be an analogous
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation"} deformation
            of that of non-abelian
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Tseytlin97"} Tseytlin 97
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Myers99"} Myers 99
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+theory"} string theory
            of this non-abelian DBI action is lacking; and it is in fact known to be in conflict, beyond the first few orders of correction terms, with effects argued elsewhere in the string theory literature (
            %a{:href => "#HashimotoTaylor97"}> Hashimoto-Taylor 97
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Bain99"} Bain 99
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#BergshoeffBilalRooSevrin01"} Bergshoeff-Bilal-Roo-Sevrin 01
          %p
            When the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            in question are interpreted as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"} flavor branes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electric+field"} electric field
            which arises from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/DBI-action"} DBI-action
            has been argued (
            %a{:href => "#SemenoffZarembo11"}> Semenoff &amp; Zarembo 2011
            ) to reflect, via
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holographic+QCD"} holographic QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+limit"} Schwinger limit
            beyond which the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vacuum+polarization"} vacuum polarization
            caused by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electromagnetic+field"} electromagnetic field
            leads to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deconfinement"} deconfinement
            of
            = succeed "." do
