                        \\tfrac{2\cdot 2}{4!}
                        \\delta^{a_3 a_4}_{b_3 b_4}
                        F_{a_3 b_3} F_{a_4 b_4}
                        \\;=\;
                        \- \sum_{a, b} F_{a b} F_{a b}
                %p
                  where we used that due to the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/skew-symmetric+matrix"} skew-symmetry
                  of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                  the first case in
                  %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:TheRelativeLCTensor"} (4)
                  does not contribute, only the second case does.
                %p
                  Now it just remains to translate this back to the situation at hand where we use
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi η
